From f90b489d3f1ae017315cea077243087daa66c6a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:18:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] [TSReader] Take the PTS diff of the segment of each
 frame

The demuxer emits a frame after later PES packets start, so a frame can
come after the segment change, and an audio frame can come after the
video of the next segment. With one frame per segment, the segment
changes twice before the frame is a sample. One diff change per segment
gave these frames the diff of the wrong segment.

The demuxer now tags each PES with its segment, and each sample takes
the diff of its own segment: the PTS of the first video PES of the
segment, or of the first PES without video, minus the segment offset.
The first offset belongs to the segment of the stream information. An
audio frame before the first video PES of its segment keeps the diff of
the segment before; HLS starts a new period at a discontinuity, so the
segments of a reader are continuous.

A seek also lands on the frame of the seek time:
- Without video, the seek found a frame inside an audio PES, but the
  read started at the first frame of the PES. The read now skips the
  frames of that stream before the frame.
- With video, an audio frame after the seek time ended the scan before
  the key frame of the seek time. Now only video frames end the scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
